{
 "decisions": [
  "Excluded tags: tags whose content MediaWiki does not render as wikitext (nowiki, pre, syntaxhighlight, source, math, chem, ce, score, timeline, graph, mapframe, maplink, templatedata, includeonly, inputbox, categorytree, charinsert, hiero). Identifier-shaped text inside them is recorded as excluded, never used.",
  "Unsupported containers: gallery, poem, imagemap, noinclude, onlyinclude. A ref inside them is kept and reported.",
  "DOI-bearing URLs: a URL names a DOI when its host is a DOI resolver (doi.org, dx.doi.org) or its path has a /doi/ segment (optionally /doi/abs/, /full/, /pdf/, /epdf/, /book/, /reader/) followed by 10.<registrant>/; the development corpus showed this publisher-platform convention on hosts beyond the first five seen in Stage 01/02 evidence, so it is not limited to a host list. Other URL shapes are not decoded (no request is made to decide). A DOI path ending in a page-view segment (/abstract, /full, /pdf and similar) is kept with an ambiguous boundary.",
  "Warning terms: the literal words the marker templates write ('Retracted', 'expression of concern', 'مصدر مسحوب'), plus the adjective 'مسحوب/مسحوبة' and English 'retracted' on arwiki, where dev renders show the English word written by hand ('(Retracted)' in فضيحة شون). Ambiguous terms are wording that may or may not be a warning (a cited title, 'Retraction Watch', withdrawal of a drug, an erratum).",
  "Preprint DOI fields: the CS1 bioRxiv and medRxiv identifier parameters (handlers BIORXIV and MEDRXIV) hold the full DOI of the preprint version of the cited work, so they are DOI fields of the citation template. When a template also has doi=, the two DOIs are co-reported (CO_REPORTED_IDENTIFIERS); neither is chosen.",
  "Missing templates: Retracted, Expression of concern and Erratum do not exist on arwiki (evidence: missing pages); they stay in the arwiki marker list because articles copy them from enwiki and the render then shows a red link (missing_template_link_only)."
 ],
